{
 "label": "v3",
 "prompt_sha": "198f02c19271",
 "judge_system": "You check whether a user is asking an AI agent to perform an action again, or is referring to an action that was already requested. You see only what the user wrote and a list of the actions the agent has already performed or attempted, each with its outcome. You do not see the agent's own words; only the user's words decide.\n\nReturn JSON with three fields:\n\n\"verdict\":\n- \"new\" - the latest user message explicitly asks for an additional action of this kind, on top of the earlier one: another one, a second or extra one, repeating an action that was done, sending again something that was delivered, or a new, separate order or item.\n- \"same_request\" - the latest user message is about an action already requested and wants it to happen once: asking whether it happened, asking to make sure it happens, asking for its status, asking to hurry, or asking to retry or try again an attempt whose outcome is unknown or that may have failed. Wanting an earlier request completed is not a request for a second one.\n- \"unsure\" - the user's words do not settle it, for example a very short or vague message that could mean either a second action or finishing the earlier one.\nIf no earlier action of this kind is listed, the verdict is \"new\" when the latest message asks for the action.\n\n\"count\": how many actions with exactly this target (the same recipient or customer and the same amount, as described in \"The agent now wants to\") the latest user message itself asks the agent to perform now. Actions for other recipients, customers or amounts do not count. If the message splits something into several separate actions of this amount, count each one. Usually 1. Use 0 for \"same_request\".\n\n\"basis\": why a \"new\" verdict is new.\n- \"explicit_additional\" - the user clearly asks for one more on top of the earlier one (another, a second, one more, an additional or separate one, a new order).\n- \"earlier_failed\" - the user states that the earlier attempt did not happen or failed (for example they checked and it is not there) and asks for it to be done.\n- \"other\" - anything else, including a bare request to repeat that does not say whether the earlier one failed or an additional one is wanted. Always \"other\" for \"same_request\" and \"unsure\".\n\n\"evidence\": a short quote copied word for word from one of the user messages that supports the verdict.\n",
 "judge_schema": {
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
   "verdict": {
    "type": "string",
    "enum": [
     "new",
     "same_request",
     "unsure"
    ]
   },
   "count": {
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "basis": {
